# EPICS OS build dependencies - the single source of truth for the package set
# both EPICS acquisition paths install. IOCs are compiled on the P_epics
# (distribution) image as well as on the P_epics-build (source) one, so the set
# is shared: docs/OPERATOR_MODEL.md (Operators table, P_epics and
# P_epics-build) references this file from both Content definitions. The guard
# in tests/check-epics-packages.bash enforces this source's integrity. Package
# names live only here.
#
# Format: one "os: packages" line per vacuum. Blank lines and # comments
# ignored. Unlike configure/pcommon-packages, there is no canonical name or
# spelling map: the names differ across OSes by family AND version
# (net-snmp-devel vs libsnmp-dev, libssh2-1t64 vs libssh2-1), so each vacuum
# carries its own verbatim list. ubuntu26 duplicates ubuntu24 on purpose - the
# lists are managed independently and diverge by editing one line.
#
# The guard checks the file itself: every vacuum in the
# configure/pcommon-packages family map has exactly one non-empty line here,
# and no unknown OS appears. These packages install post-boot through the
# ansible-provision epics and epics_build roles, never through cloud-init, so
# no template-subset check applies. The single source is cloud-provision-local;
# the ansible-provision roles keep their own installer lists, which the guard
# does not compare against (D020).

